# Type 1 §2 #5 (iii): two incompatible specifications of unit-table row 7, four lines apart

`combined-analyzer-optimizer-design.md` specifies the scale-down tie-break
(`sortVariantsForScaleDown`, bug #5 site (iii), unit-table row 7) twice in the same bullet, and the
two specifications select different analyzers. Routed here per Dean (2026-08-07) — the Type 1 is
`Status: FINAL` and the reviewer owns it.

| where | says |
|---|---|
| `:1177-1179` | "Fix: tie-break on the ***binder's*** PRC (which requires the function to learn which role it is ordering), name-ascending as the final key, and give a variant with no scale-down ballot at all the same key today's weighted sum yields for that input, so that edge does not move." |
| `:1181-1186` (blockquote, 4 lines later) | "The unit of this key is **dimensionless — coverage per GPU freed**… it must combine across analyzers with **`max_i`, not `Σ_i`**" |
| `:2482` (unit table row 7) | "**none — coverage per GPU freed**; dimensionless ratio; `max_i`, not `Σ_i`." |

## Why these are not two wordings of one rule

For `up=false`, `combineVotes`' binder is the entry with the **minimum** `spare/prc`
(`analyzer_helpers.go:369-380`). That coincides with the maximum-PRC entry only when every voter's
spare happens to be equal. And the "binder's PRC" formulation never mentions the
`GPUsPerReplica` division that row 7's *per GPU freed* unit requires — without it the key is a raw
PRC and is not dimensionless at all.

So `:1177-1179` and `:1181-1186`/`:2482` are different keys, not different phrasings.

## What the coder did, and why it was right

It resolved by the documented precedence (Type 1 governs; the Type 3's §2d.5 tie-break rule points
the same way) and implemented the blockquote: `maxᵢ PRC_i[v] ÷ GPUsPerReplica[v]` ascending, then
name ascending, Score absent. Landed in `330fcd26` (C6d) at
`cost_aware_optimizer.go:183-217`. It matches `:1181-1186` and row 7 at `:2482`.

## One clause of `:1177-1179` is still live and should survive any strike

The third clause — *"give a variant with no scale-down ballot at all the same key today's
weighted sum yields for that input, so that edge does not move"* — **is honored** by the
implementation and is not stale: `coveragePerGPU` initializes `best = 0.0`
(`cost_aware_optimizer.go:188-204`), which is what the old empty weighted sum also produced, so a
variant nothing can price keeps its key. Only the *mechanism* clause ("the binder's PRC", and the
parenthetical about learning the role) is contradicted. Striking the sentence wholesale would drop
a requirement the code satisfies.

